gm.sf3: the shared General MIDI sounds that every tool which plays MIDI uses,
so they all sound the same.

It is made from GeneralUser GS 2.0.3 by S. Christian Collins
(http://www.schristiancollins.com), under the GeneralUser GS License v2.0,
reproduced in full below. The licence lets
the bank be used in software projects and modified.

What was changed (make-soundfont.mjs, beside this file, rebuilds it from the
original GeneralUser.sf2):
- kept the 128 General MIDI programs of bank 0 and the Standard 1 drum kit
  (keys 27-87); the GS variation banks and other kits were removed;
- 38 programs play a close sibling's instrument instead of their own (for
  example Viola plays the Violin, the pads play Polysynth), listed in the
  tool's ALIAS table;
- unlooped samples longer than 2 seconds end there, with a 0.4 s fade;
- samples longer than a few KB are stored as Ogg Vorbis (SoundFont 3,
  libvorbis quality 3); short ones stay 16-bit PCM.

This file is our own copy, as the licence asks: please link to
schristiancollins.com for the original, not to his download files.

